<h2 id="included">What is included in the plans?</h2>
<p>Growth is the entry point for a team that needs the core help desk. It is not just a bare inbox: Freshdesk lists ticketing, a customer portal, knowledge base capabilities and reporting in its plan materials. Still, check the exact feature matrix for your account type because Freshdesk and Freshdesk Omni have different channel coverage.</p>
<p>Pro is the tier to examine when your team needs more routing and reporting control. Freshworks lists custom dashboards, intelligent routing and multiple SLA policies among the capabilities associated with higher plans. Enterprise adds controls such as audit logs and sandbox features. Plan names and included features can change, so treat this table as a decision guide rather than a contract.</p>
<h2 id="extras">AI and other costs that can change the bill</h2>
<p>Seat price is only one part of the cost. The current pricing page lists the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions as included and shows US$49 for each additional 100 sessions. The visible pricing summary does not make every allowance condition clear, so confirm the period, counting rules and overage terms with Freshworks before budgeting.</p>
